& [RefinementSubject] is SOP's proposed identity as a multi-target semantic programming language
  + [source_impulse] is an LLM can help turn articulated SOP meaning into neural fabric and executable instruction
  + [refined_center] is SOP articulates intended meaning as typed semantic programs that may compile into proof-carrying exact, neural, hybrid, and derived projections
  + [authority_boundary] is purpose formation only

& [StableTermMap] is integrated
  + [SOP] means source-preserved semantic articulation under explicit context, role, contract, and authority
  + [SemanticProgram] means an explicitly admitted program region composing typed operations under one complete SemanticContract
  + [SemanticIR] means the canonical source-mapped, target-neutral semantic representation
  + [compile] means validate and project accepted meaning into one or more target artifacts without executing it
  + [exact] means deterministic semantics whose claimed behavior is completely governed by inspectable contracts and proof obligations
  + [neural] means learned, stochastic, embedding-routed, or provider-mediated behavior whose outputs remain qualified proposals
  + [hybrid] means exact control and admission around bounded neural proposal behavior
  + [neural_printer] means generation of a blueprint, candidate initial state, corpus contract, training/evaluation plan, or packaged learned target, not magical direct correctness
  + [execution] means admitted evaluation of a SemanticProgram and remains distinct from compilation, proposal, authorization, and effect commitment
  + [target] means a versioned projection profile behind the CommonTargetABI
  + [PackageFamily] means content-bound related target artifacts derived from one SemanticIR root
  + [conformance] means independent evidence that a surface form, target, or implementation satisfies its declared semantic boundary
  + [fallback] means valid exact behavior remains available without acceptance of a neural result
  + [self_hosting] means SOP can describe compiler contracts while retaining an independently trusted bootstrap

& [RoleRefinement] preserves historical meaning
  + [source_document] preserves raw human or imported expression
  + [definition] supplies identities and relations
  + [data] supplies inspectable values or observations
  + [contract] supplies constraints without self-activation
  + [program] alone is an executable candidate after all gates
  + [policy] governs admission without self-execution
  + [profile] narrows language or target behavior without conferring authority
  + [test_or_fixture] executes only in an isolated harness
  + [proof] records evidence without becoming the proved fact
  + [narrative] preserves reasoning and reentry without execution
  + [package_manifest] binds lineage without becoming a program
  + [mixed] requires exact region boundaries and is non-executable by default

& [RejectedConflationSet] is binding
  + LLM_compiler is not deterministic compiler
  + neural_weights are not authoritative SOP records
  + embedding_similarity is not semantic identity or declared subtype
  + parser_success is not semantic validity
  + compiler_success is not runtime admission
  + signature_metadata is not cryptographic trust by itself
  + signed_definition is not executable program
  + target_artifact is not executed event
  + proposal is not judgment acceptance
  + judgment acceptance is not effect authority
  + source_relevance is not capability grant
  + read_capability is not write capability
  + valid_form is not truthful observation
  + generated_model is not trained_or_evaluated_model
  + generated_weight_candidate is not semantic_equivalence
  + self_description is not self_validation
  + hardware_projection is not FPGA implementation
  + concise_contract is not omitted_dependency_permission

& [InferenceControlRefinement] keeps the language inspectable
  + attention operations modify an explicit AttentionFrame rather than hidden model state authority
  + inference operations produce typed judgments under named regimes
  + constraints accept, qualify, challenge, reject, or preserve unresolved material
  + transforms preserve source correspondence and declare semantic loss
  + controls bind branches, loops, yields, returns, stops, and budgets
  + effects remain requests until authorized and committed through a broker
  + emitted results distinguish value, proposal, proof, fault, observation, and artifact

& [CrossWeave_ExistingCore] is compatible
  + SOP Semantic Programming Identity already establishes source, SemanticIR, program, contract, and target distinctions
  + SOP Core already defines explicit program admission and semantic instruction families
  + Attention First Language Foundation supplies the base attention, inference, control, and effect primitives
  + Reflective Virtual Machine supplies transition, trace, and runtime separation
  + Neural Compilation Boundary makes learned output advisory and derived
  + Trusted Compilation Profile separates SJS metadata from cryptographic package admission
  + Semantic Fabric Graph supplies typed contextual temporal graph identity
  + Proof Carrying Query Engine supplies query results with evidence rather than bare retrieval

& [CrossWeave_WorkerProofs] closes purpose gaps
  + WS-CTPR-002 contributes explicit document and region roles, ten admission gates, mixed-document closure, and historical compatibility
  + WS-CTPR-003 contributes language profiles, role-first passes, kinds, types, effects, modules, standard-library boundary, optimizer laws, TargetABI, RuntimeABI, diagnostics, and conformance
  + both remain derived worker evidence until the canonical signature binds them

& [UncertaintyLedger] preserves what purpose formation does not settle
  + exact grammar productions remain LanguageProfile artifacts
  + exact standard-library membership remains module-source work
  + physical parser, compiler, runtime, database, cache, and serialization designs remain implementation work
  + neural topology and weight initialization remain target-profile experiments
  + target equivalence strength depends on each target's later proof
  + FPGA interpreter versus native synthesis remains a target-profile decision
  + no current evidence proves an LLM can preload correct learned weights directly from arbitrary SOP
  + no current evidence proves the full language or compiler is implemented

& [IntegrationExpression] is the refined statement
  + SOP is a source-preserving semantic programming language whose explicit programs compile through one role-checked SemanticIR into exact and derived target artifacts with declared loss, proof, authority, compatibility, and runtime boundaries
  + LLM assistance may form candidate artifacts but cannot self-authorize their meaning or effects
  + purpose authority makes these distinctions governing for future specification; it does not release implementation

& [RefinementCheck] passes
  + [identity_preserved] is true
  + [uncertainty_preserved] is true
  + [source_overwrite] is false
  + [authority_widening] is false
  + [loop_inflation_result] is stable after role, execution, neural, target, and bootstrap distinctions were made explicit
  + [remaining_semantic_collision] is none within current purpose scope
